From 54db51dbd55d1cab1a3dc053222f4f20a0f38477 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joe Mason <joenotcharles@google.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:09:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Reland "Return only live tabs from TabRestoreService restore operations"

This reverts commit a467c37711d44556022a49dbbbce6b1d4bda8964.

Reason for revert: Fixed MSAN errors

Original change's description:
> Revert "Return only live tabs from TabRestoreService restore operations"
>
> This reverts commit b10218380b91df1c63d4eb1a8d4ad50adfa22ea7.
>
> Reason for revert: Newly added tests are failing
>
> Failure Link:
> https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/ci/Linux%20ChromiumOS%20MSan%20Tests/61349/overview
>
> https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/ci/Linux%20MSan%20Tests/64914/overview
>
>
> Original change's description:
> > Return only live tabs from TabRestoreService restore operations
> >
> > TabRestoreService restore methods previously collected raw LiveTab
> > pointers before showing and activating the target browser window.
> > If showing the window triggers nested event processing that closes
> > restored tabs or the window before the operation completes, the
> > returned collection could include pointers to destroyed tabs.
> >
> > Track restored tabs using WeakPtr throughout the restore pipeline and
> > filter out any tabs that are no longer valid upon completion. In
> > addition, update SessionsRestoreFunction to handle empty restore results
> > gracefully by returning an error instead of assuming a tab is always
> > present.
> >
> > Fixed: 553132214
